e-boundary-audit.json","source_file_sha256":"99525c575faeca278bbca79377ff85df6a3c53ad2e71cf66fdea37e5a8ac917d","rank_eligible":false,"label":"Indian SECC 2013 source stops and unresolved threshold edges","figure":"figures/indian-secc-source-boundaries-2013/index.html"},{"id":"diagnostic:red-sea-ozgokmen-2003-width-scope","current_id":"red-sea-saline-overflow","entity_id":"current:red-sea-saline-overflow","kind":"primary_source_channel_dimension_scope","document":{"schema":"osw.current-primary-source-review.v1","current_id":"red-sea-saline-overflow","reviewed_on":"2026-10-22","citation":"Özgökmen, T. M., W. E. Johns, H. Peters and S. Matt (2003), Turbulent Mixing in the Red Sea Outflow Plume from a High-Resolution Nonhydrostatic Model, Journal of Physical Oceanography 33, 1846–1869","doi":"10.1175/2401.1","source_identity":{"source_url":"http://www.tamayozgokmen.org/ftp-pub/jpo03.pdf","discovery_url":"http://www.tamayozgokmen.org/index2.html","acquisition_receipt":"research/source-data/ozgokmen-redsea-2003/acquisition.json","bytes":1482243,"sha256":"888d26defac366e3992ef93894883d17a0f7ae7346d87e18bbeaefd961c30aa3","pdf_pages":24,"printed_pages":"1846–1869","original_redistributed":false,"rights":"American Meteorological Society, 2003. No redistribution permission inferred; original and page renders remain private."},"review_scope":{"kind":"selected_primary_pages_not_full_paper_review","visually_verified_pdf_pages_1_based":[1,3,4,5],"printed_pages":[1846,1848,1849,1850],"text_search_scope":"All 24 pages searched for width and lateral confinement; search hits alone are not measurement admissions.","figure_digitized":false},"findings":[{"locator":"p. 1848, section 2; p. 1849, Figure 1","finding":"Approximately 100 km length and 3 km width at overflow depth describe the Northern Channel.","consequence":"Retain bathymetric context, not a whole-current dimension or paired velocity-edge measurement."},{"locator":"p. 1846, abstract; p. 1848, section 2","finding":"The winter investigation concerns one confined branch after the overflow splits.","consequence":"Neither dimension represents all Red Sea outflow branches or downstream spreading."},{"locator":"p. 1850, section 3a–b","finding":"The model resolves along-channel and vertical dynamics; lateral edge effects and canyon-wall intrusions are omitted.","consequence":"Its two-dimensional solution does not recover lateral velocity boundaries."},{"locator":"p. 1849, Figure 1 and caption","finding":"The highlighted paths are schematic branch and station context.","consequence":"No observed current axis, footprint or length digitized from this figure."}],"reported_channel_context":{"branch_id":"redsox-northern-channel-plume","approximate_channel_length_km":100,"channel_width_at_overflow_depth_km":3,"exact_section_location":null,"exact_width_sampling_date":null,"velocity_edge_definition":null,"geometry":null,"rank_eligible":false},"cross_source_rule":{"related_review":"research/red-sea-redsox-branch-reach-scope-audit.json","rule":"Do not combine the 3 km and prior 5 km channel descriptions into a current-width uncertainty or seasonal envelope. Matching sections, depth definitions, measurement methods and dates have not been established.","prior_records_rewritten":false},"physical_width_admitted":false,"physical_axis_admitted":false,"physical_length_admitted":false,"annual_width_range_admitted":false,"next_measurement_gate":"Recover dated cross-flow velocity sections with both lateral plume boundaries and depth/layer support; admit branch scope before attributing any result to the parent current."},"source_file":"research/ozgokmen-2003-red-sea-width-scope-review.json","source_file_sha256":"356a8a833d957c171bd7ca2ebeee92d40adbbfae99cba063bf8e7e7734c1d9c9","rank_eligible":false,"label":"Red Sea 2003 channel dimensions are not measured plume widths"},{"id":"diagnostic:neuc-glider-2015-width-ranges","label":"NEUC glider jet width ranges: two local jets","entity_id":"current:pacific-north-equatori